### ... dispatched before it: the write that schedules it makes the timer's `when` false and cancels it
# @name DispatchWo7102
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/commands/work-orders/{{CreateWo7102.response.body.$.id}}/dispatch
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "{{userSpareNorth}}", "startsAt": "2027-03-02T09:00:00Z", "durationMinutes": 60 }

### WO-7101 as the dispatcher sees it — polled until the host's `escalate-sla-breach` handler raised it, at most ~30 s
# @name ReadWo7101
## RETRY-UNTIL-TEST-PASS: WO-7101 escalated to priority 1.
## RETRY-MAX-ATTEMPTS: 30
## RETRY-BACKOFF-TYPE: Constant
## RETRY-MAX-DELAY: 00:00:01
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{CreateWo7101.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
